/api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/8647","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/8647"}},{"id":"893487","ext":"jpg","post_id":"897031","description":null,"caption":null,"poi_name":null,"subject":null,"author":"Philip Young","poi_id":null,"photo_date":"2020-09-04T14:45:56.000Z","updated_at":"2022-08-22T14:45:56.000Z","url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/893487","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/893487"}},{"id":"893486","ext":"jpg","post_id":"897030","description":null,"caption":null,"poi_name":null,"subject":null,"author":"Philip Young","poi_id":null,"photo_date":"2020-09-04T14:47:24.000Z","updated_at":"2022-08-22T14:47:24.000Z","url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/893486","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/893486"}}],"detail":{"id":"1923","permitUrl":null,"permitInfo":null,"description":"This is a great trip, with beautiful scenery and good water quality.  Although there isn't a lot of whitewater, the current moves along well and there are plenty of riffles and small wave trains.  The main rapid is a small ledge (II or II+) about a mile downstream from Griffith.  Run on the left side with a little left angle.  Two other spots may be worth mentioning for novices.  First, after passing under the I-64 bridges, there is a third bridge (Longdale Furnace Rd.) where the main current flows directly into a bridge piling (see the gallery for what can happen here).  However, it's easy to see from upstream and move to the right.  Second, about a mile downstream, there is an island where most of the flow goes left.  Near the end of the island, the flow accelerates and pushes into a cliff on the left.  This can be avoided with some right angle and a little paddling.\n\nAlternate accesses are at Sharon park (5 mi.) and Evans Tract (10 mi.), where the gauge is located.  Generally 600-700 is the minimum for putting in at the Griffith ford.\n\nSee Also:\n\n_Virginia Whitewater_, Roger Corbett (2000 ed.), p. 250.\n\n_Exploring Virginia's Waterways_, Ed Gertler (2022 ed.), p. 180.","averageGradient":"10","maxGradient":"0","length":"13","correlations":[{"reachID":"1923","isPrimary":true,"correlationDetails":{"metric":"cfs","belowRecommendedRangeComment":null,"lowRunnableRangeComment":null,"mediumRunnableRangeComment":null,"highRunnableRangeComment":null,"aboveRecommendedRangeComment":null,"lowRunnableAdjustedDifficulty":null,"highRunnableAdjustedDifficulty":null,"beginLowRunnable":"600","beginMediumRunnable":"800","beginHighRunnable":"2000","endHighRunnable":"20000"},"gaugeInfo":{"name":"COWPASTURE RIVER NEAR CLIFTON FORGE, VA","gaugeSource":"USGS","gaugeSourceIdentifier":"02016000","gaugeFetchStatus":"ACTIVE","latestFlowReading":{"value":"199","dateTime":"2026-05-12T02:30:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"latestStageReading":{"value":"1.8","dateTime":"2026-05-12T02:30:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"location":{"latitude":"37.79179587","longitude":"-79.7594917"},"externalSourceLinks":{"sourceLink":{"url":"https://water.noaa.gov/gauges/02016000","text":"NOAA"},"secondaryLink":{"url":"https://waterdata.usgs.gov/monitoring-location/02016000/#parameterCode=00060&period=P7D","text":"US Geological Survey"}}},"migrationErrorExplanation":null,"comment":"Gauge (Drainage = 461 sq.mi.) is well down toward the take-out for this reach, thus should accurately show flow in this reach.","status":{"status":"below-recommended","latestReading":{"value":"199","dateTime":"2026-05-12T02:30:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"metric":"cfs","adjustedDifficulty":null}}],"pointOfInterestIDs":["109922","YmaZzTwmx6c53gs5uyqHx","XQHM6Ny72renWNZTa3zpR","ojVR82pt7XDqgQVwmodnB","115174"],"geometry":{"type":"LineString","coordinates":[[-79.734239,37.866475],[-79.734703,37.866223],[-79.734821,37.866096],[-79.734821,37.866096],[-79.735293,37.863979],[-79.735269,37.863845],[-79.735261,37.863846],[-79.735139,37.863161],[-79.735043,37.8